  "body": "### What problem are you trying to solve?\n\nRunning script when a select element's picker is opened or closed\n\n### What solutions exist today?\n\nFor opening the picker you could add event listeners to the select element itself to detect clicks or keyboard inputs which might open the picker. This would require incorporating platform differences and looking at the event's patch to see whether the event originated in the picker or not.\n\nFor closing the picker you could add click and keyboard event listeners to the whole document or document.body, and guess whether they will close the picker or not. The same challenges for opening still apply, but it would likely be even harder to figure out whether the event will close the picker.\n\n### How would you solve it?\n\nAdd toggle and beforetoggle events to the select element which get fired when the picker is toggled open or closed.\n\nThis would have been possible for customizable select with an earlier propsed design which allowed the author to provide their own popover element as a datalist element, but since we removed that capability it is no longer possible to listen to toggle and beforetoggle events directly on the popover since it is in a user-agent shadowroot.\n\nThis was raised in OpenUI here: https://github.com/openui/open-ui/issues/1228\n\n### Anything else?\n\n_No response_",
